msgid ""
"Unix style wildcarding is accepted:\n"
"Most characters match themselves\n"
"A \"?\" will match any single character\n"
"A \"*\" will match an arbitrary number of characters (including none)\n"
"An \"[abd]\" set of characters within square brackets will match any (single) character\n"
"A \"{scmp,c2sc}\" set of strings within curly brackets will match any string\n"
"So \"a.*\" would match \"a.\" or \"a.sc\" or \"a.swash\"\n"
"While \"a.{scmp,c2sc}\" would match \"a.scmp\" or \"a.c2sc\"\n"
"And \"a.[abd]\" would match \"a.a\" or \"a.b\" or \"a.d\""
msgstr ""
"Unix-liknande jokertecken accepteras:\n"
"De flesta tecken matchar sig själva\n"
"Ett \"?\" matchar alla enskilda tecken\n"
"En \"*\" matchar ett godtyckligt antal tecken (inklusive inget)\n"
"En \"[abd]\"-uppsättning tecken inom hakparenteser matchar alla (enskilda) tecken\n"
"En \"{scmp,c2sc}\"-uppsättning strängar inom hakparenteser matchar vilken sträng som helst\n"
"Så \"a.*\" skulle matcha \"a.\" eller \"a.sc\" eller \"a.swash\"\n"
"Medan \"a.{scmp,c2sc}\" skulle matcha \"a.scmp\" eller \"a.c2sc\"\n"
"Och \"a.[abd]\" skulle matcha \"a.a\" eller \"a.b\" eller \"a.d\""

